so there's some debate about whether or  not orcs must die Unchained is a MOBA  now i'm not a big MOBA player so i'm not  in the best position to determine  whether the various elements that  comprise orcs must die unchain make the  game ova or not and in the end I'm not  sure it matters when I got to play  unchanged last week in advance of the  games beta my feeling was that it's a  more accessible game than something like  League of Legends our dota while still  having enough facets to allow for deep  rewarding tactical play it probably  helped my experience that I spent most  of my time playing as blackpaw a  powerful and agile offensive hero with  whom I could confidently leap into the  fray and deal damage to enemy minions  and players  unlike in a traditional MOBA minions  aren't generic units that are  automatically generated and sent or the  enemy base instead each team has war  camps where you play cards from your  deck to determine what types of minions  are sent forth minions have all kinds of  different characteristics some are pure  damage dealers others disable traps  others heal and putting together a more  effective combination of minions than  the opposing team is important since  victory goes to the first team that gets  20 minions into the rift in the opposing  teams fortress  as you play you earn leadership points  which can either be poured into  upgrading existing war camps enabling  them to send out more powerful minions  or into opening up new war camps  allowing you to assault the enemy team  down multiple lanes on the defensive  side there's the traditional orcs must  die element of traps you can spend gold  you earn during the match on traps  designed to prevent enemy minions from  getting anywhere near your rift and  placing traps like choosing minions is a  tactical concern because certain types  of traps work better against certain  types of minions the action moves fast  and between offense/defense setting  traps choosing minions and upgrading war  camps there's a lot to think about I had  fun during the three matches I played  but whether these elements make  unchained a game that can stand out in  the increasingly crowded world of  competitive online games remains to be  seen the game is in beta now so if you  want a shot at checking it out for  yourself you can go to the official site  and sign up  I
 

